course: dictionary
lesson: 14014
title: Short words in casual talk
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mag is a short, casual word. It is a clipped form of magazine, and people shorten long words when they chat, text or talk fast. When you meet a short word, ask what the full word might be and check it against the words around it.
explain: «I bought a football mag at the shop, full of pictures and match stories.» A thin book of pictures and articles that comes out regularly is a magazine, so mag must mean magazine here. Swap the full word into the sentence: «I bought a football magazine» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Words also show how a speaker feels. Mag is informal, so it sounds relaxed and friendly, like talking to a mate. You would write «magazine» in a school report, but you might text «mag» to a friend. Clipped words tell you the speaker is casual.
fact: Mag is short for magazine: a thin book with pictures and articles that comes out regularly.
fact: Mag is informal, so you use it in chatty talk and texts, not in school essays.
fact: In older Australian and British speech, «to mag» means to chat or gossip for a long time.
fact: Mag can also mean the part of a gun that holds the bullets.
fact: In science, «Mg» is the symbol for magnesium, a metal.
exercise: «She read her favourite football mag on the bus.» What does mag mean? | A loud noise | A ball kicked in a match | A small dog | *A magazine with pictures and articles
exercise: Mum and her friends had a mag over the fence for an hour. What does mag mean here? | Cleaned the garden | *Chatted or gossiped | Ran a race | Shouted angrily
exercise: Why does a writer use mag instead of magazine in a text message? | *Because it is a quick, casual short word | Because it is the only correct spelling | Because it means a very big book | Because it is a type of car
test:
«The new gaming mag has a free poster inside.» What is a mag here? | *A magazine | A computer game | A gaming console | A school bag
Which symbol stands for magnesium in science? | Mx | Ma | Gm | *Mg
exam:
Ella says «I'll grab a mag for the train.» What is she most likely to grab? | *A thin magazine full of pictures and articles | A train ticket | A fishing rod | A bag of crisps
